22634","id":1170622634,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/9641","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5Fxkiq","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1170622634/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-06-30T00:32:03Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1170622634","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4314836?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/okkwon","id":4314836,"login":"okkwon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMTQ4MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4314836?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/okkwon","id":4314836,"login":"okkwon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMTQ4MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4314836?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/okkwon","id":4314836,"login":"okkwon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMTQ4MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"### What happened?\n\nThe dispatch with the fused reduction and elementwise op references a same buffer with different shape and the bufferization's `findOrCreateSubspanBuffer()` returns a wrong one.\r\n\r\nWe have two subspans for <1001xf32> and <1x1001xf32> which are mapped to the same input buffer. While doing the bufferization, memref<1001xf32> is created, and it is found again for the second subspan, and returned. Since the types are different, the verifier reports an error later.\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ iree-opt --iree-codegen-iree-comprehensive-bufferize dispatch_72.mlir\r\ndispatch_72.mlir:20:10: error: 'linalg.generic' op expected operand rank (1) to match the result rank of indexing_map #0 (2)\r\n    %9 = linalg.generic {indexing_maps = [affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0, d1)>, affine_map<(d0, d1) -> ()>, affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0, d1)>], iterator_types = [\"parallel\", \"parallel\"]} ins(%5, %8 : tensor<1x1001xf32>, tensor<f32>) outs(%3 : tensor<1x1001xf32>) {\r\n         ^\r\ndispatch_72.mlir:20:10: note: see current operation: \"linalg.generic\"(%4, %12, %7) ({\r\n^bb0(%arg0: f32, %arg1: f32, %arg2: f32):\r\n  %17 = \"arith.divf\"(%3, %arg1) : (f32, f32) -> f32\r\n  %18 = \"arith.mulf\"(%arg0, %17) : (f32, f32) -> f32\r\n  \"linalg.yield\"(%18) : (f32) -> ()\r\n}) {indexing_maps = [affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0, d1)>, affine_map<(d0, d1) -> ()>, affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0, d1)>], iterator_types = [\"parallel\", \"parallel\"], operand_segment_sizes = dense<[2, 1]> : vector<2xi32>} : (memref<1001xf32>, memref<f32>, memref<1x1001xf32>) -> ()\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ cat dispatch_72.mlir                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \r\nmodule {\r\n  func.func @main_dispatch_72() {\r\n    %c5120 = arith.constant 5120 : index\r\n    %c0 = arith.constant 0 : index\r\n    %cst = arith.constant 0.000000e+00 : f32\r\n    %cst_0 = arith.constant 1.000000e+00 : f32\r\n    %0 = hal.interface.binding.subspan set(0) binding(0) type(storage_buffer) offset(%c5120) alignment(64) : !flow.dispatch.tensor<readonly:1001xf32>\r\n    %1 = hal.interface.binding.subspan set(0) binding(0) type(storage_buffer) offset(%c5120) alignment(64) : !flow.dispatch.tensor<readonly:1x1001xf32>\r\n    %2 = hal.interface.binding.subspan set(0) binding(1) type(storage_buffer) offset(%c0) alignment(64) : !flow.dispatch.tensor<writeonly:1x1001xf32>\r\n    %3 = flow.dispatch.tensor.load %2, offsets = [0, 0], sizes = [1, 1001], strides = [1, 1] : !flow.dispatch.tensor<writeonly:1x1001xf32> -> tensor<1x1001xf32>\r\n    %4 = flow.dispatch.tensor.load %0, offsets = [0], sizes = [1001], strides = [1] : !flow.dispatch.tensor<readonly:1001xf32> -> tensor<1001xf32>\r\n    %5 = flow.dispatch.tensor.load %1, offsets = [0, 0], sizes = [1, 1001], strides = [1, 1] : !flow.dispatch.tensor<readonly:1x1001xf32> -> tensor<1x1001xf32>\r\n    %6 = bufferization.alloc_tensor() : tensor<f32>\r\n    %7 = linalg.fill ins(%cst : f32) outs(%6 : tensor<f32>) -> tensor<f32>\r\n    %8 = linalg.generic {indexing_maps = [affine_map<(d0) -> (d0)>, affine_map<(d0) -> ()>], iterator_types = [\"reduction\"]} ins(%4 : tensor<1001xf32>) outs(%7 : tensor<f32>) attrs =  {lowering_config = #iree_codegen.lowering_config<tile_sizes = [[0]]>} {\r\n    ^bb0(%arg0: f32, %arg1: f32):\r\n      %10 = arith.addf %arg0, %arg1 : f32\r\n      linalg.yield %10 : f32\r\n    } -> tensor<f32>\r\n    %9 = linalg.generic {indexing_maps = [affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0, d1)>, affine_map<(d0, d1) -> ()>, affine_map<(d0, d1) -> (d0, d1)>], iterator_types = [\"parallel\", \"parallel\"]} ins(%5, %8 : tensor<1x1001xf32>, tensor<f32>) outs(%3 : tensor<1x1001xf32>) {\r\n    ^bb0(%arg0: f32, %arg1: f32, %arg2: f32):\r\n      %10 = arith.divf %cst_0, %arg1 : f32\r\n      %11 = arith.mulf %arg0, %10 : f32\r\n      linalg.yield %11 : f32\r\n    } -> tensor<1x1001xf32>\r\n    flow.dispatch.tensor.store %9, %2, offsets = [0, 0], sizes = [1, 1001], strides = [1, 1] : tensor<1x1001xf32> -> !flow.dispatch.tensor<writeonly:1x1001xf32>\r\n    return\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\n\n_No response_\n\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_at":"2022-07-13T00:22:49Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4314836?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okkwon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.gi